1
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:07,320
Lazy Meow Meow,
is competing at Siam for the first time!

2
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:11,240
<i>I'm glad we're talking</i>
<i>like we used to again.</i>

3
00:00:11,320 --> 00:00:13,000
<i>Just getting your support</i>

4
00:00:13,080 --> 00:00:15,720
<i>was enough to help me chase my dream.</i>

5
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:16,920
<i>I came over to say hi, LeeIth.</i>

6
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:20,320
<i>I think, this one isn't hiding it.</i>

7
00:00:20,840 --> 00:00:22,040
<i>I think</i>

8
00:00:22,120 --> 00:00:23,240
<i>you might have feelings for Jia.</i>

9
00:00:23,320 --> 00:00:25,040
<i>Honestly, I feel that way too.</i>

10
00:00:25,120 --> 00:00:27,120
If you ever feel sad, just be sad.

11
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:28,680
<i>People can't control their feelings.</i>

12
00:00:28,760 --> 00:00:31,120
<i>Besides Indy, you're my best friend too.</i>

13
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:34,240
I'm going back to Chiang Mai.

14
00:00:35,040 --> 00:00:36,320
Tell Mom and Dad for me.

15
00:00:50,440 --> 00:00:52,040
Stop acting cool. Hurry up.

16
00:00:53,680 --> 00:00:55,680
- I know.
- Hurry up. Come on.

17
00:01:03,560 --> 00:01:04,599
Okay, let's go.

18
00:01:26,760 --> 00:01:30,240
Mom, I wish you good health
and that you get prettier every day.

19
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:32,120
How sweet.

20
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:34,440
And I hope you get
a thousand times richer,

21
00:01:34,520 --> 00:01:36,000
so we can finally travel abroad together.

22
00:01:36,080 --> 00:01:37,200
Huh?

23
00:01:37,920 --> 00:01:38,960
Hey, Sis.

24
00:01:39,040 --> 00:01:41,120
You've lived abroad for ages.
What more do you want?

25
00:01:41,200 --> 00:01:43,440
Well, I went alone. I'm bored of that.

26
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:45,320
Next time, we all have to go together.

27
00:01:47,080 --> 00:01:49,840
Okay, great. All right, everyone,
let's sing together.

28
00:01:55,800 --> 00:01:56,720
I'll blow out the candles now.

29
00:02:36,400 --> 00:02:38,160
What is this? You're creeping me out.

30
00:02:38,240 --> 00:02:40,120
Let me get a photo with the hot guy.

31
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:42,720
You just transferred
to Watthana Kunlaya School,

32
00:02:42,800 --> 00:02:44,560
and you already gained
a thousand followers.

33
00:02:44,640 --> 00:02:45,720
I'm so confused.

34
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:49,080
Well, this super handsome guy

35
00:02:49,160 --> 00:02:50,520
is your little brother.

36
00:02:57,160 --> 00:03:00,000
Hey, have you told Mom and Dad yet?

37
00:03:03,720 --> 00:03:04,600
Not yet.

38
00:03:05,760 --> 00:03:07,080
I'll help you.

39
00:03:07,160 --> 00:03:08,960
- No!
- Mom, Dad,

40
00:03:09,040 --> 00:03:10,520
Lee wants to talk to you.

41
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:12,640
- Wait a second.
- Go ahead.

42
00:03:14,960 --> 00:03:16,160
What is it, sweetheart?

43
00:03:22,320 --> 00:03:23,400
Mom.

44
00:03:23,480 --> 00:03:24,480
Yes, honey?

45
00:03:25,560 --> 00:03:26,760
Well,

46
00:03:27,840 --> 00:03:29,760
I wanted to ask,

47
00:03:30,600 --> 00:03:32,960
if I really want to be a musician,

48
00:03:34,440 --> 00:03:36,040
would you mind?

49
00:03:40,880 --> 00:03:44,160
I'll be honest, I'm hesitant too.

50
00:03:45,400 --> 00:03:48,640
Because you're the type
to get bored with things quickly.

51
00:03:51,560 --> 00:03:53,840
But when I saw you onstage,

52
00:03:56,080 --> 00:03:59,600
I realized what truly makes you happy.

53
00:04:01,040 --> 00:04:02,280
Onstage?

54
00:04:03,720 --> 00:04:04,920
When did you see that?

55
00:04:05,560 --> 00:04:06,960
Mom shared it all over Facebook.

56
00:04:07,040 --> 00:04:08,240
Didn't you see it?

57
00:04:08,960 --> 00:04:10,160
Facebook?

58
00:04:10,240 --> 00:04:11,440
Who even uses that anymore?

59
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:13,360
Only old people use Facebook.

60
00:04:13,440 --> 00:04:17,240
Well, it's old people like us
who support our kids.

61
00:04:19,040 --> 00:04:21,560
That Instagram thing is too hard.

62
00:04:21,640 --> 00:04:23,960
We aunties aren't good with it.

63
00:04:24,040 --> 00:04:27,280
We just follow the links your mom shares.

64
00:04:27,880 --> 00:04:28,800
But you're good.

65
00:04:28,880 --> 00:04:30,080
You even came in second.

66
00:04:30,160 --> 00:04:32,000
- Yeah, that's right.
- Amazing.

67
00:04:32,520 --> 00:04:35,320
Great job, Son.
I even liked it on Facebook.

68
00:04:38,560 --> 00:04:40,920
Wait, you all saw it?

69
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:43,360
Yeah, we all saw it.

70
00:04:43,440 --> 00:04:45,280
And I'm so proud of you.

71
00:04:46,800 --> 00:04:50,520
If you want to study music,
I'll support you.

72
00:04:51,200 --> 00:04:52,200
I only ask one thing.

73
00:04:52,280 --> 00:04:54,200
Don't do anything halfheartedly.

74
00:04:56,040 --> 00:04:57,760
You can do it, Son. I'm rooting for you.

75
00:04:58,280 --> 00:05:00,960
Aw, Mom, Dad.

76
00:05:01,040 --> 00:05:02,400
Don't make me emotional.

77
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:04,440
You're so sensitive.

78
00:06:21,720 --> 00:06:22,880
Dad, look.

79
00:06:27,760 --> 00:06:28,680
Here.

80
00:06:32,040 --> 00:06:32,880
Huh?

81
00:06:32,960 --> 00:06:34,440
Aren't you taking it to the uncles?

82
00:06:35,160 --> 00:06:36,160
It's for you.

83
00:06:36,240 --> 00:06:39,480
Practice so you'll know your limit,
how much it takes to get you drunk.

84
00:06:41,800 --> 00:06:42,640
Here.

85
00:06:48,720 --> 00:06:50,680
It's so damn bitter.
How do you guys drink this?

86
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:54,120
When you grow up, it'll taste sweet.

87
00:06:54,200 --> 00:06:55,080
That's right.

88
00:06:55,160 --> 00:06:57,560
Because once life's bitter,
a cold beer is the best thing ever.

89
00:06:58,640 --> 00:07:00,040
That's a bit much.

90
00:07:01,040 --> 00:07:02,800
I'll take this to the uncles.

91
00:07:07,440 --> 00:07:08,440
Hi.

92
00:07:09,080 --> 00:07:11,240
Want some snacks too, you drunks?

93
00:07:11,320 --> 00:07:13,440
You started drinking before sunset.

94
00:07:17,640 --> 00:07:20,840
Seriously, is there anything else
you want to tell us?

95
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:24,520
We've already talked about school,

96
00:07:25,120 --> 00:07:27,040
and we can talk about love too.

97
00:07:33,480 --> 00:07:35,240
- I…
- Wait.

98
00:07:35,320 --> 00:07:37,160
I'll take them some snacks first.

99
00:07:37,240 --> 00:07:38,880
I'll be back. Wait for me.

100
00:07:44,200 --> 00:07:45,840
We're back.

101
00:07:46,640 --> 00:07:47,840
Okay, we're ready.

102
00:07:55,200 --> 00:07:57,760
That's enough. You'll get drunk
and we won't understand you.

103
00:07:57,840 --> 00:07:58,960
- Dad, you too.
- Huh?

104
00:08:10,040 --> 00:08:13,240
Well, I'm wondering…

105
00:08:15,520 --> 00:08:17,560
When you date a friend

106
00:08:19,360 --> 00:08:20,200
and you break up,

107
00:08:22,520 --> 00:08:24,080
then go back to being friends,

108
00:08:25,720 --> 00:08:27,240
but no matter what,

109
00:08:27,320 --> 00:08:29,680
you can't really be friends
with your ex again.

110
00:08:32,159 --> 00:08:33,720
Dad, Mom, Sis, what would you do?

111
00:08:34,559 --> 00:08:37,039
Don't tell me you dated Indy.

112
00:08:38,039 --> 00:08:40,320
I'm gonna puke. No.

113
00:08:41,600 --> 00:08:44,680
I bet it's Putter.

114
00:08:46,120 --> 00:08:47,400
Right?

115
00:08:50,160 --> 00:08:53,240
I've known for ages.
I was waiting for you to tell us.

116
00:08:54,160 --> 00:08:55,240
At least it's not Indy.

117
00:08:55,880 --> 00:08:57,360
That's not the point, Dad.

118
00:08:59,880 --> 00:09:01,320
But I like Putter.

119
00:09:02,640 --> 00:09:05,880
He seems serious and more responsible.

120
00:09:06,480 --> 00:09:07,560
His grades are good.

121
00:09:07,640 --> 00:09:10,000
He studies hard and still does activities.

122
00:09:11,480 --> 00:09:13,400
Is there anything you don't know, Mom?

123
00:09:15,440 --> 00:09:19,400
So, you guys don't mind

124
00:09:21,040 --> 00:09:22,560
that I like…

125
00:09:28,560 --> 00:09:30,920
These days,
there's nothing strange about it.

126
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:33,560
Like whoever you want. We don't mind.

127
00:09:35,200 --> 00:09:36,120
Just like your dad.

128
00:09:36,760 --> 00:09:40,200
The moment he saw me,
he knew I was the one.

129
00:09:40,280 --> 00:09:43,480
Then he chased after me,
and here we are 20 years later.

130
00:09:43,560 --> 00:09:45,600
Come on, you're really feeling yourself.

131
00:09:45,680 --> 00:09:47,960
Shouldn't Dad be the one
telling that story, Mom?

132
00:09:50,400 --> 00:09:53,720
Whoever you date,
if they hold you back in life,

133
00:09:54,240 --> 00:09:56,360
that's when we'd see it as a problem.

134
00:09:59,480 --> 00:10:01,080
Talk to Putter again.

135
00:10:01,680 --> 00:10:03,280
Try to understand each other,

136
00:10:03,360 --> 00:10:05,000
and don't force yourself.

137
00:10:05,600 --> 00:10:08,280
If you still like him,
just tell him you like him.

138
00:10:09,120 --> 00:10:10,400
But if you don't, don't force it.

139
00:10:10,480 --> 00:10:12,360
If you don't want to be friends,
that's okay too.

140
00:10:12,440 --> 00:10:14,480
Forcing it will only hurt everyone, right?

141
00:10:14,560 --> 00:10:15,720
No one will be happy.

142
00:11:14,240 --> 00:11:15,320
Te.

143
00:11:15,840 --> 00:11:17,120
Is Putter with you?

144
00:11:17,640 --> 00:11:19,680
<i>No, he's not. Why?</i>

145
00:11:44,800 --> 00:11:46,200
<i>He's flying back to Chiang Mai,</i>

146
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:48,560
<i>and it looks like he's not coming back.</i>

147
00:11:48,640 --> 00:11:50,360
What? He's not coming back?

148
00:11:51,640 --> 00:11:54,000
Do you know his flight number and time?

149
00:11:59,040 --> 00:12:00,160
TAXI

150
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:16,080
Hello?

151
00:13:16,720 --> 00:13:17,760
Where are you?

152
00:13:18,280 --> 00:13:19,440
Lee.

153
00:13:24,200 --> 00:13:25,680
What are you doing here?

154
00:13:58,360 --> 00:14:01,200
Putter, I'm sorry.

155
00:14:02,840 --> 00:14:04,080
For what?

156
00:14:04,160 --> 00:14:06,440
Wait. Have you been drinking beer?

157
00:14:07,720 --> 00:14:10,640
You see, I really can't
be friends with you.

158
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:14,640
I'm the kind of person who,
once I love someone, I love them.

159
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:19,560
And how I feel right now
is more than friendship.

160
00:14:19,640 --> 00:14:21,240
That's easy for you to say.

161
00:14:21,760 --> 00:14:23,040
I saw you've moved on.

162
00:14:23,560 --> 00:14:24,880
I saw you talking to someone new.

163
00:14:24,960 --> 00:14:27,600
No, I was talking to Chompoo

164
00:14:27,680 --> 00:14:29,760
because she's with a record label,

165
00:14:29,840 --> 00:14:31,440
and I just want an internship.

166
00:14:31,520 --> 00:14:32,640
Seriously.

167
00:14:32,720 --> 00:14:34,040
Believe me.

168
00:14:38,360 --> 00:14:40,400
What about the matching keychains?

169
00:14:40,920 --> 00:14:43,360
You even crumpled up
the picture I drew for you.

170
00:14:48,680 --> 00:14:50,360
<i>That's because</i>
<i>I was trying to get over you.</i>

171
00:14:52,680 --> 00:14:54,120
<i>But I just can't.</i>

172
00:14:54,800 --> 00:14:56,440
<i>Because every time I'm around you</i>

173
00:14:57,440 --> 00:14:59,120
<i>and try to be just friends,</i>

174
00:15:03,720 --> 00:15:04,920
<i>I still can't move on.</i>

175
00:15:11,280 --> 00:15:14,200
I'm begging you.
Don't run away to Chiang Mai.

176
00:15:14,800 --> 00:15:16,040
Give me another chance.

177
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:19,000
I mean…

178
00:15:22,880 --> 00:15:24,240
You and me,

179
00:15:26,480 --> 00:15:27,760
can we get back together?

180
00:15:42,040 --> 00:15:43,480
I'm not running away from you.

181
00:15:45,480 --> 00:15:47,560
Honestly, I'm the same as you.

182
00:15:49,160 --> 00:15:50,840
I really can't go back
to being your friend.

183
00:15:53,080 --> 00:15:56,480
But, I still have to go home.

184
00:15:56,560 --> 00:15:57,840
Huh?

185
00:15:57,920 --> 00:16:00,360
Why? Won't you give me a chance?

186
00:16:01,080 --> 00:16:02,320
It's not like that.

187
00:16:04,200 --> 00:16:05,480
I mean,

188
00:16:05,560 --> 00:16:08,160
if we feel the same,
you don't have to go back, right?

189
00:16:08,240 --> 00:16:09,840
Listen to me first.

190
00:16:09,920 --> 00:16:12,400
- Don't be so cruel to me.
- Listen to me first.

191
00:16:14,880 --> 00:16:16,160
I just have to go see my grandma.

192
00:16:20,960 --> 00:16:22,600
<i>Are you on break yet?</i>

193
00:16:23,680 --> 00:16:25,080
<i>Grandma's in the hospital.</i>

194
00:16:25,160 --> 00:16:27,520
ARE YOU ON BREAK YET?
GRANDMA'S IN THE HOSPITAL.

195
00:16:31,520 --> 00:16:34,960
I'm going back to Chiang Mai.
Tell Mom and Dad for me.

196
00:16:38,040 --> 00:16:39,480
But I still have to go back.

197
00:16:40,720 --> 00:16:42,400
I've already booked my ticket too.

198
00:16:42,480 --> 00:16:44,240
I thought you were mad at me,

199
00:16:44,320 --> 00:16:46,600
so you were getting back at me
by moving back to Chiang Mai.

200
00:16:49,040 --> 00:16:52,000
But Te said you weren't coming back here.

201
00:16:52,080 --> 00:16:53,040
What's that about?

202
00:16:55,800 --> 00:16:57,880
I might have to transfer schools.

203
00:16:58,960 --> 00:16:59,920
Transfer schools?

204
00:17:01,080 --> 00:17:02,320
I'm still not sure.

205
00:17:02,960 --> 00:17:06,119
But I'll go talk to my family
and rethink my future.

206
00:17:06,200 --> 00:17:09,400
Because, architecture isn't for me anyway.

207
00:17:11,319 --> 00:17:14,079
But if your dream is to play esports,

208
00:17:15,040 --> 00:17:16,480
can't you stay here?

209
00:17:18,560 --> 00:17:21,280
Well, if my family isn't okay with it,

210
00:17:22,359 --> 00:17:24,720
I… might not come back here.

211
00:17:37,080 --> 00:17:38,920
At least I know you feel the same way.

212
00:17:40,840 --> 00:17:42,520
No matter what happens,

213
00:17:45,600 --> 00:17:48,160
I'll always be your number one supporter.

214
00:17:52,920 --> 00:17:55,560
I… don't want you to wait for me.

215
00:17:56,560 --> 00:17:57,480
No.

216
00:17:58,120 --> 00:17:59,800
Call me stubborn if you want,

217
00:18:00,760 --> 00:18:01,760
but I'll wait for you.

218
00:18:02,960 --> 00:18:04,560
I'll wait until you come back.

219
00:18:07,120 --> 00:18:08,160
And we'll…

220
00:18:11,240 --> 00:18:12,520
get back together.

221
00:18:16,360 --> 00:18:18,400
But if your family won't let you,

222
00:18:19,320 --> 00:18:20,800
I'll go straight to your house.

223
00:18:23,400 --> 00:18:24,760
I'll sort it out myself.

224
00:18:26,640 --> 00:18:28,320
You really won't give up, will you?

225
00:18:28,400 --> 00:18:29,880
You're so damn stubborn.

226
00:18:29,960 --> 00:18:31,080
So…

227
00:18:32,680 --> 00:18:33,720
what's your answer?

228
00:18:35,680 --> 00:18:36,800
Figure it out yourself.

229
00:18:36,880 --> 00:18:38,040
It's pretty obvious.

230
00:18:55,440 --> 00:18:56,680
Thanks, Putter.

231
00:18:58,760 --> 00:18:59,760
Yeah.

232
00:19:00,360 --> 00:19:01,600
I'll video call you.

233
00:19:02,200 --> 00:19:04,120
But I'm gonna miss my flight now.

234
00:19:04,720 --> 00:19:05,560
It's okay.

235
00:19:05,640 --> 00:19:07,000
I'll buy you a new ticket.

236
00:19:08,400 --> 00:19:09,480
You talk like you're rich.

237
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:12,640
If you really have money,
why not buy a ticket and come with me?

238
00:19:14,520 --> 00:19:16,160
- I'm going now.
- Yeah.

239
00:19:36,240 --> 00:19:38,800
I'm off. Good luck. Bye.

240
00:19:44,120 --> 00:19:46,040
Wanna take a trip during break?

241
00:19:46,120 --> 00:19:47,400
<i>How about the beach?</i>

242
00:19:48,240 --> 00:19:49,480
Will your family let you go?

243
00:19:50,600 --> 00:19:51,680
No problem.

244
00:19:51,760 --> 00:19:53,800
I can help Mom at home afterward.

245
00:19:54,760 --> 00:19:57,560
So, you're talking to me,

246
00:19:57,640 --> 00:19:58,760
but you're not talking to Faye?

247
00:19:59,480 --> 00:20:00,960
I don't know what to say to her.

248
00:20:05,200 --> 00:20:06,040
That's weird.

249
00:20:07,120 --> 00:20:07,960
What?

250
00:20:09,560 --> 00:20:10,440
The Lovers card fell out.

251
00:20:12,640 --> 00:20:15,240
Does that mean
you're gonna have a girlfriend?

252
00:20:15,320 --> 00:20:18,040
<i>Well, if it's about love,</i>

253
00:20:18,880 --> 00:20:20,200
<i>it's like I'm about to find something new.</i>

254
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:23,440
But it's also about making a choice.

255
00:20:23,520 --> 00:20:25,440
If I choose wrong, I'm screwed.

256
00:20:27,880 --> 00:20:30,360
But, it's probably nothing.

257
00:20:46,360 --> 00:20:49,720
I don't think dating someone close to you
is a good idea.

258
00:20:50,520 --> 00:20:52,440
<i>Someday, there might be problems.</i>

259
00:20:52,520 --> 00:20:54,480
<i>But the biggest shame is…</i>

260
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:57,600
losing the friendship.

261
00:21:13,640 --> 00:21:14,520
I…

262
00:21:18,400 --> 00:21:19,400
I think

263
00:21:20,160 --> 00:21:23,400
the Lovers card is trying
to tell me something.

264
00:21:26,360 --> 00:21:27,800
You suddenly came to see me.

265
00:21:27,880 --> 00:21:29,360
Did you miss me?

266
00:21:32,480 --> 00:21:33,440
Faye.

267
00:21:34,600 --> 00:21:36,040
What's wrong, Indy?

268
00:21:37,240 --> 00:21:39,240
I have something to tell you.

269
00:21:45,520 --> 00:21:47,520
I don't have romantic feelings for you.

270
00:21:50,320 --> 00:21:52,160
Did I do something wrong?

271
00:21:53,240 --> 00:21:54,440
Faye, you did nothing wrong.

272
00:21:54,960 --> 00:21:59,040
It's just, I was so excited
about dating you,

273
00:21:59,720 --> 00:22:02,600
but once we actually did,
I realized it wasn't love.

274
00:22:03,640 --> 00:22:05,640
So I don't want you to get hurt

275
00:22:05,720 --> 00:22:09,040
or waste your time… on me.

276
00:22:11,480 --> 00:22:13,400
Is it really that simple?

277
00:22:18,680 --> 00:22:20,000
I'm sorry.

278
00:22:20,520 --> 00:22:21,760
I was wrong.

279
00:22:32,840 --> 00:22:33,960
Let's break up.

280
00:22:36,240 --> 00:22:37,800
But just so you know,

281
00:22:37,880 --> 00:22:42,480
I'm the one breaking up with you,
not you dumping me.

282
00:22:56,160 --> 00:22:57,760
How dare you break up with my sister?

283
00:22:58,760 --> 00:23:00,320
You're exactly like your friend.

284
00:23:03,760 --> 00:23:06,840
Faye, you're better off
without someone like him.

285
00:23:10,480 --> 00:23:11,680
Goodbye.

286
00:23:11,760 --> 00:23:13,200
Stop chasing after my sister.

287
00:23:13,280 --> 00:23:17,440
FOOD - LETTER - PACKAGE

288
00:23:22,560 --> 00:23:23,640
Yes!

289
00:23:38,840 --> 00:23:42,160
<i>Loving yourself never hurts.</i>

290
00:23:42,240 --> 00:23:45,240
<i>Some people are like waste in your body.</i>

291
00:23:45,320 --> 00:23:47,240
You need to detox them all out.

292
00:23:47,760 --> 00:23:49,400
Let's take better care of ourselves.

293
00:23:51,440 --> 00:23:52,520
Whoa.

294
00:23:53,520 --> 00:23:54,640
- Damn.
- Shit.

295
00:23:54,720 --> 00:23:57,080
You became a meme overnight.

296
00:23:59,200 --> 00:24:00,160
Look.

297
00:24:02,360 --> 00:24:03,680
My life is over.

298
00:24:06,680 --> 00:24:08,120
It's not just you, dude.

299
00:24:08,840 --> 00:24:10,400
I'm getting dragged into this too.

300
00:24:10,920 --> 00:24:13,720
<i>This group of guys is something else.</i>

301
00:24:13,800 --> 00:24:15,800
<i>Change the name from</i>
<i>"You'll Get Used to It"</i>

302
00:24:15,880 --> 00:24:17,480
<i>to "You'll Just Be Worthless."</i>

303
00:24:24,040 --> 00:24:25,120
Come on.

304
00:24:25,920 --> 00:24:27,160
Your planet's in retrograde.

305
00:24:28,240 --> 00:24:31,600
It's a time when things swept
under the rug tend to come out.

306
00:24:35,200 --> 00:24:37,040
What's been swept under the rug?

307
00:24:38,200 --> 00:24:42,360
Like, unresolved feelings,

308
00:24:42,440 --> 00:24:45,280
the truth, things like that.

309
00:24:49,160 --> 00:24:50,200
Wait.

310
00:24:51,200 --> 00:24:53,000
Lee got back together with Putter,

311
00:24:54,280 --> 00:24:56,200
and Indy broke up with Faye.

312
00:24:56,720 --> 00:24:58,640
Shit.

313
00:24:59,360 --> 00:25:01,480
The universe is for real, fortune teller.

314
00:25:03,600 --> 00:25:04,920
I'll read your cards for you.

315
00:25:05,440 --> 00:25:06,680
I'll give you 50% off.

316
00:25:07,200 --> 00:25:09,160
Didn't you say you were
afraid I'd get hooked on tarot,

317
00:25:09,240 --> 00:25:10,360
so you wanted me to live my own life?

318
00:25:10,440 --> 00:25:12,120
I've diagnosed you,

319
00:25:12,640 --> 00:25:14,360
and your condition is too severe.

320
00:25:15,440 --> 00:25:16,520
Fine.

321
00:25:17,040 --> 00:25:18,920
Maybe I should get a reading from you.

322
00:25:28,000 --> 00:25:28,880
What?

323
00:25:29,480 --> 00:25:31,120
You guys, get out.

324
00:25:31,200 --> 00:25:32,840
Jia needs to concentrate.

325
00:25:35,240 --> 00:25:37,520
Did he forget this is my room?

326
00:25:45,160 --> 00:25:48,280
Pick three cards
and ask them what you want to know.

327
00:25:50,520 --> 00:25:54,360
Well, love, I guess.

328
00:26:06,320 --> 00:26:08,320
You're still naive about love.

329
00:26:09,360 --> 00:26:11,800
You might need to be braver
to move forward.

330
00:26:13,720 --> 00:26:17,520
Hey, the cards say you'll find pure love.

331
00:26:20,040 --> 00:26:21,920
New opportunities are coming your way.

332
00:26:24,160 --> 00:26:26,240
So, do the cards say

333
00:26:26,760 --> 00:26:28,720
if it's a close friend
or someone close to me?

334
00:26:33,200 --> 00:26:34,160
Why?

335
00:26:34,960 --> 00:26:36,640
Do you like someone close to you?

336
00:26:39,160 --> 00:26:40,280
I guess.

337
00:26:45,800 --> 00:26:47,040
How close?

338
00:26:53,960 --> 00:26:55,200
One foot.

339
00:27:05,240 --> 00:27:06,520
Ten centimeters.

340
00:27:12,280 --> 00:27:13,400
Five centimeters.

341
00:27:40,160 --> 00:27:41,120
Isn't that too close?

342
00:27:47,160 --> 00:27:48,320
Dude,

343
00:27:49,360 --> 00:27:52,520
they've got some serious chemistry.

344
00:27:53,720 --> 00:27:55,480
You're really into this, aren't you?

345
00:27:55,560 --> 00:27:59,480
I guess I've been around Min too much.

346
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:01,160
I'm so into this.

347
00:28:01,240 --> 00:28:02,640
Hashtag "JiaIn."

348
00:28:02,720 --> 00:28:07,320
- Or should it be hashtag "InJia"?
- Stop shaking me!

349
00:28:07,840 --> 00:28:08,760
Fine.

350
00:28:19,480 --> 00:28:20,600
Hello, babe.

351
00:28:20,680 --> 00:28:21,680
Where is everyone else?

352
00:28:22,200 --> 00:28:24,240
Everyone else?
I don't want them seeing you.

353
00:28:24,920 --> 00:28:25,760
I'm possessive.

354
00:28:25,840 --> 00:28:27,320
Possessive of what?

355
00:28:27,400 --> 00:28:29,800
<i>What? With a cute face like yours,</i>

356
00:28:29,880 --> 00:28:31,440
how could I not be?

357
00:28:32,840 --> 00:28:33,920
Oh, right.

358
00:28:34,000 --> 00:28:35,440
When are you coming back?

359
00:28:35,520 --> 00:28:36,720
I'm dying here.

360
00:28:37,440 --> 00:28:39,240
Just count down till I come back.

361
00:28:39,320 --> 00:28:41,280
I don't know when I'll be back yet.

362
00:28:41,360 --> 00:28:45,040
Oh, have you talked to your parents yet
about school?

363
00:28:48,520 --> 00:28:49,880
Not yet.

364
00:28:49,960 --> 00:28:51,880
I haven't found the right time.

365
00:28:51,960 --> 00:28:53,400
I don't know when to bring it up.

366
00:28:54,240 --> 00:28:55,440
<i>You know that</i>

367
00:28:57,320 --> 00:28:58,840
I'm always on your side, right?

368
00:29:04,040 --> 00:29:05,320
Give me your address.

369
00:29:05,400 --> 00:29:06,760
I'll send you some food.

370
00:29:06,840 --> 00:29:08,080
Stop it.

371
00:29:08,160 --> 00:29:11,280
Since I came back here,
I've been eating so much healthy food.

372
00:29:11,360 --> 00:29:13,000
Hey, don't get too skinny.

373
00:29:13,520 --> 00:29:15,560
I won't have your puppy belly to pinch.

374
00:29:16,320 --> 00:29:18,160
You're so mean.

375
00:29:19,160 --> 00:29:20,600
- Hey.
- What?

376
00:29:20,680 --> 00:29:23,200
Are you not gonna let us
talk to Putter at all?

377
00:29:23,840 --> 00:29:24,960
Hi, Putter.

378
00:29:26,280 --> 00:29:28,880
Putter, I want some pork rinds.
Bring me some.

379
00:29:30,480 --> 00:29:32,480
Hey, I'm talking to my boyfriend.

380
00:29:32,560 --> 00:29:33,640
Go away.

381
00:29:34,960 --> 00:29:35,840
<i>Go.</i>

382
00:29:35,920 --> 00:29:39,200
Wow, you can call him your boyfriend
so easily now.

383
00:29:39,280 --> 00:29:40,680
<i>Yeah.</i>

384
00:29:40,760 --> 00:29:41,600
<i>Something stinks.</i>

385
00:29:42,280 --> 00:29:43,800
Must be the smell of love.

386
00:29:43,880 --> 00:29:45,200
These two too.

387
00:29:45,280 --> 00:29:47,520
Oh, yeah. What's going on with these two?

388
00:29:47,600 --> 00:29:50,680
- Hey, stop pinching me.
<i>- Do it again.</i>

389
00:30:13,960 --> 00:30:15,920
Wow, that smells so good.

390
00:30:17,760 --> 00:30:19,240
It's a grain salad, sweetheart.

391
00:30:19,320 --> 00:30:21,520
I saw them make it in a vertical drama.

392
00:30:21,600 --> 00:30:23,440
It looked good, so I tried making it.

393
00:30:23,520 --> 00:30:24,920
Just a minute, sweetheart.

394
00:30:32,040 --> 00:30:33,240
Why are you standing there?

395
00:30:33,880 --> 00:30:34,920
Is something wrong?

396
00:30:40,040 --> 00:30:41,880
Dad. Mom.

397
00:30:43,560 --> 00:30:45,520
I don't want to study
architecture anymore.

398
00:30:53,040 --> 00:30:56,040
I understand.
You don't have to rush, Putter.

399
00:30:56,120 --> 00:30:57,840
You still have two years.

400
00:30:59,000 --> 00:31:00,640
That's not what I mean, Mom.

401
00:31:00,720 --> 00:31:04,120
I mean, I've found something I want to do,

402
00:31:04,200 --> 00:31:06,080
but I don't know
if you'll be okay with it.

403
00:31:12,240 --> 00:31:13,440
Here.

404
00:31:16,440 --> 00:31:19,440
<i>- Fire Storm!</i>
- Oh, Do you compete in esports too?

405
00:31:19,520 --> 00:31:20,960
Yeah.

406
00:31:21,040 --> 00:31:22,480
That's a big match

407
00:31:22,560 --> 00:31:24,280
I just won.

408
00:31:26,800 --> 00:31:28,240
If it makes you happy,

409
00:31:28,760 --> 00:31:30,440
I'll support you all the way.

410
00:31:31,440 --> 00:31:32,440
Right, honey?

411
00:31:41,000 --> 00:31:42,040
Putter,

412
00:31:42,120 --> 00:31:44,000
if you don't want to study architecture,

413
00:31:44,080 --> 00:31:47,480
why not try business or engineering?

414
00:31:50,880 --> 00:31:52,280
Maybe, Mom.

415
00:31:52,880 --> 00:31:55,440
But, I have my own dream now.

416
00:31:56,680 --> 00:31:58,320
I want to be an esports player.

417
00:31:59,240 --> 00:32:00,920
I enjoy playing games.

418
00:32:03,080 --> 00:32:04,760
I'm not saying you can't, Putter.

419
00:32:05,280 --> 00:32:07,240
I see you playing games all the time.

420
00:32:09,040 --> 00:32:10,600
I'm just worried

421
00:32:11,640 --> 00:32:13,400
that if you choose this path,

422
00:32:13,480 --> 00:32:15,440
what will your future look like?

423
00:32:16,920 --> 00:32:18,040
I understand, Mom.

424
00:32:23,080 --> 00:32:25,560
Take it easy.
We can talk about this later.

425
00:32:31,160 --> 00:32:34,400
Mom's probably shocked
because you just dropped that on her.

426
00:32:36,200 --> 00:32:37,680
I didn't know how to tell them.

427
00:32:39,680 --> 00:32:40,960
What about those prep classes?

428
00:32:41,040 --> 00:32:42,200
Didn't you like them at all?

429
00:32:42,720 --> 00:32:44,320
It's not that I didn't like them.

430
00:32:45,240 --> 00:32:46,840
They were fun.

431
00:32:49,120 --> 00:32:51,160
But playing games excites me more.

432
00:32:57,400 --> 00:32:59,000
Pim, here.

433
00:33:01,280 --> 00:33:03,280
I guess that's your passion.

434
00:33:03,800 --> 00:33:06,400
It's good that you know what you like.

435
00:33:08,560 --> 00:33:09,600
Yeah.

436
00:33:11,560 --> 00:33:12,560
Done.

437
00:33:15,640 --> 00:33:18,160
Putter, play for me sometime.

438
00:33:18,240 --> 00:33:19,680
I like watching game streams too.

439
00:33:20,600 --> 00:33:22,080
You know about streamers too?

440
00:33:23,240 --> 00:33:24,960
I'm waiting to send you coins, Putter.

441
00:33:26,400 --> 00:33:27,680
Thanks.

442
00:33:28,960 --> 00:33:31,240
Don't worry too much.
Mom will come around.

443
00:33:32,280 --> 00:33:33,880
Pink, come play downstairs with me.

444
00:33:35,240 --> 00:33:36,200
Thanks, guys.

445
00:33:36,280 --> 00:33:38,080
- Let's go.
- Good luck, Putter.

446
00:33:38,160 --> 00:33:39,320
Thank you, little Sis.

447
00:33:54,160 --> 00:33:55,800
<i>I talked to my parents.</i>

448
00:33:55,880 --> 00:33:57,280
<i>It didn't go too well.</i>

449
00:34:00,680 --> 00:34:03,120
<i>When you're free, give me a call.</i>

450
00:34:05,400 --> 00:34:06,760
Where did he go?

451
00:34:39,080 --> 00:34:41,920
Hello? Where the hell have you been?

452
00:34:42,440 --> 00:34:46,840
<i>Is your house</i>
<i>the one with the big black gate?</i>

453
00:34:47,360 --> 00:34:49,120
Yeah. How did you know?

454
00:34:51,000 --> 00:34:52,520
Thank you.

455
00:34:53,280 --> 00:34:55,960
Wow, your whole family is good-looking.

456
00:34:56,560 --> 00:34:58,240
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

457
00:35:05,640 --> 00:35:09,440
Thank you so much
for always looking after Putter.

458
00:35:09,520 --> 00:35:10,480
Oh,

459
00:35:10,560 --> 00:35:12,400
we should be thanking Putter.

460
00:35:12,480 --> 00:35:15,920
He's the one who keeps LeeIth in line.

461
00:35:16,000 --> 00:35:17,400
Without Putter,

462
00:35:17,480 --> 00:35:19,880
Lee would never have
straightened himself out.

463
00:35:20,800 --> 00:35:22,400
You're ruining my image.

464
00:35:23,400 --> 00:35:24,280
But it's true, isn't it?

465
00:35:24,360 --> 00:35:26,720
Otherwise, would you
have gotten serious enough

466
00:35:26,800 --> 00:35:29,560
to become a trainee at a record label?

467
00:35:30,240 --> 00:35:32,200
Wait, they accepted you?

468
00:35:32,280 --> 00:35:33,600
Yeah.

469
00:35:35,120 --> 00:35:37,240
But honestly, it was Putter

470
00:35:37,320 --> 00:35:41,040
who made me realize
that following your dreams is possible.

471
00:35:43,080 --> 00:35:44,480
Honestly,

472
00:35:44,560 --> 00:35:49,200
at first, I was the one who wasn't sure

473
00:35:49,280 --> 00:35:52,680
if playing music
would give him a stable future.

474
00:35:53,480 --> 00:35:57,040
I sent him to Watthana Kunlaya School
because I wanted him to be a doctor.

475
00:35:58,000 --> 00:36:00,520
But when I saw him playing music and…

476
00:36:01,080 --> 00:36:02,880
how happy he was,

477
00:36:03,400 --> 00:36:04,680
I thought,

478
00:36:04,760 --> 00:36:07,120
how could I stop him?

479
00:36:09,400 --> 00:36:11,960
<i>Oh, you compete in esports too?</i>

480
00:36:12,640 --> 00:36:13,880
Yeah.

481
00:36:13,960 --> 00:36:15,400
That's a big match

482
00:36:15,480 --> 00:36:17,160
I just won.

483
00:36:18,320 --> 00:36:21,920
If it makes you happy,
I'll support you all the way.

484
00:36:22,880 --> 00:36:23,840
Right, honey?

485
00:36:30,560 --> 00:36:32,880
Then I guess it's like Putter
when he plays video games.

486
00:36:33,400 --> 00:36:35,200
He looks so happy.

487
00:36:39,120 --> 00:36:42,160
Putter, when you're close to graduating,

488
00:36:42,240 --> 00:36:44,160
if your dream is still the same,

489
00:36:46,360 --> 00:36:48,640
then I'll support you all the way.

490
00:36:50,320 --> 00:36:51,320
Really, Mom?

491
00:36:51,400 --> 00:36:52,520
Of course, sweetheart.

492
00:36:53,160 --> 00:36:56,040
But, there's one condition.

493
00:36:56,800 --> 00:36:59,640
You still have to prep for architecture,

494
00:37:00,320 --> 00:37:02,360
and keep practicing your
drawing skills just in case.

495
00:37:02,440 --> 00:37:05,600
Just think of it as a hobby.

496
00:37:06,720 --> 00:37:09,720
Of course. I'll be there
studying with him too.

497
00:37:11,040 --> 00:37:12,160
You'll only disturb him.

498
00:37:16,640 --> 00:37:18,560
You'll just distract Putter.

499
00:37:27,880 --> 00:37:29,720
We're bonding.

500
00:37:30,240 --> 00:37:32,360
We get along pretty well.

501
00:37:32,440 --> 00:37:34,360
- If I stay up too late, he complains.
- You ready?

502
00:37:34,880 --> 00:37:36,120
- I'm always ready.
- Let's go.

503
00:37:36,200 --> 00:37:37,880
- I have to turn off the big light first.
- Right?

504
00:37:39,760 --> 00:37:41,560
I can't stay up late. He always complains.

505
00:37:44,400 --> 00:37:45,480
He scolds me too.

506
00:37:45,560 --> 00:37:47,640
"Turn off the light. It hurts my eyes."

507
00:37:52,960 --> 00:37:54,560
Dad, Mom.

508
00:37:56,280 --> 00:37:57,240
I have something to tell you.

509
00:38:04,040 --> 00:38:06,560
When I first moved to Bangkok,

510
00:38:07,680 --> 00:38:10,560
I… acted like I could handle it,

511
00:38:11,080 --> 00:38:13,680
but honestly, I was scared.

512
00:38:14,760 --> 00:38:15,920
Scared I wouldn't fit in with my friends.

513
00:38:17,640 --> 00:38:19,280
Scared I'd feel like an outsider.

514
00:38:28,000 --> 00:38:29,680
But when I met Lee,

515
00:38:30,720 --> 00:38:32,480
he made all my worries disappear.

516
00:38:34,360 --> 00:38:35,960
Lee is someone important to me.

517
00:38:38,880 --> 00:38:40,760
And I want to tell you that

518
00:38:42,120 --> 00:38:43,320
Lee…

519
00:38:44,480 --> 00:38:46,200
isn't just my best friend.

520
00:38:50,440 --> 00:38:51,800
He's my boyfriend.

521
00:39:45,160 --> 00:39:48,720
Then please treat Putter like
another son of yours.

522
00:39:49,840 --> 00:39:51,600
I'd be more than happy to.

523
00:39:51,680 --> 00:39:52,880
But actually,

524
00:39:52,960 --> 00:39:55,680
I'm the one who should be leaving
Lee in Putter's hands.

525
00:39:57,080 --> 00:39:58,240
Lee,

526
00:39:58,320 --> 00:40:00,720
make sure you keep Putter in line.

527
00:40:01,760 --> 00:40:04,880
Don't let Putter neglect his studies
until he's a full-time esports player.

528
00:40:05,520 --> 00:40:06,480
Okay?

529
00:40:07,880 --> 00:40:09,440
What kind of person
do you think your son is?

530
00:40:16,560 --> 00:40:17,720
Everyone,

531
00:40:17,800 --> 00:40:20,880
let's celebrate, then.

532
00:40:23,720 --> 00:40:25,560
- Come on.
- Let's go, Mom!

533
00:40:25,640 --> 00:40:26,480
Here comes my child!

534
00:40:26,560 --> 00:40:28,160
Come on.

535
00:40:28,240 --> 00:40:29,320
Thank you.

536
00:41:11,440 --> 00:41:12,440
Hey.

537
00:41:12,520 --> 00:41:14,280
I've been thinking.

538
00:41:15,520 --> 00:41:17,360
If you're serious
